  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs an iPhone user with a large text size, I want the explanation behind a Réglages ⓘ button to be fully readable, so that a long explanation is not clipped inside a small popover.\n\n### Rule\n\n\"Avoid displaying popovers in compact views. Make your app or game dynamically adjust its layout based on the size class of the content area. Reserve popovers for wide views; for compact views, use all available screen space by presenting information in a full-screen modal view like a sheet instead.\" — [HIG › Popovers](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/popovers) (iOS, iPadOS).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/InfoBubbleButton.swift:15-16`: `.popover(isPresented: $isShown) { bubble().presentationCompactAdaptation(.popover) }`.\n- Used by four rows: `Settings/ReplyButtonRow.swift:17`, `Settings/DefaultBrowserRow.swift:11`, `Settings/SecuritySettingsSections.swift:19`, `Settings/FilterMinimumQuotesRow.swift:14`.\n- The content is several sentences with `.fixedSize(horizontal: false, vertical: true)` and no `ScrollView` (`Settings/ReplyButtonInfoView.swift:7-18`: three titled paragraphs).\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\nNo counterpart (`git grep -n \"InfoBubble\\|presentationCompactAdaptation\" 87fe0d1c -- HFRswift` is empty). The bubble is an operator decision of 2026-11-17 (#1062, #1065, #1071, #1072).\n\n### Class\n\n**(b) evolution** against a recorded operator decision; it becomes **(a)** if the Mac check shows clipped text at accessibility sizes. Same component rule as the title pill (#1153).\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- Drop `presentationCompactAdaptation(.popover)` so compact width gets the system sheet (with `.presentationDetents([.medium])`), or keep the popover and wrap the bubble in a `ScrollView`, or move the text to the section footer.\n- Mac check: iPhone, largest accessibility text size, the « Bouton + » and iCloud-sync bubbles: the whole text is reachable.\n\nRelated: #1128 (the Expérimental ⓘ).\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
